	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[script SQL : affectation de variables]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=5243#p5243"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>salut tous le monde,</p><p>mon problème comment affecter un variable dans un requête SQL dans postgresql : </p><p>dans mysql on utilise @REF := ss.commercial<br />exemple : <br />select <br />&#160; &#160; IF (ss.commercial = @REF, null, ss.commercial) as commercial, <br />&#160; &#160; ss.*,<br />&#160; &#160; @REF := ss.commercial as Curr<br />&#160; &#160; <br />from&#160; &#160; (SELECT @REF:=&#039;&#039;) AS ref,<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;(select&#160; ord.* <br />&#160; &#160; from c_order ord<br />&#160; &#160; where <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ord.ad_client_id=1000000<br />&#160; &#160; ) as ss<br />ORDER BY ss.commercial</p><p>est ce quelqu&#039;un parmi vous peux m&#039;aider ??</p><p>et merci</p>]]></content>
